{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a visible-light photoredox-catalyzed arylcarboxylation of unactivated alkenes using CO2. By employing a synergistic catalytic system of an iridium photocatalyst and a thiol HAT catalyst, the authors achieved the synthesis of various polycyclic carboxylic acids (tetrahydronaphthalenes, indanes, indolines, chromanes, and thiochromanes) under mild conditions (1 atm CO2, room temperature). The reaction proceeds via the in situ generation of a CO2 radical anion followed by radical addition to the alkene and subsequent cyclization.",
